      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Given that the roots of the polynomial \\( ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = 0 \\) are \\( 3, -2, \\) and \\( r \\), we can express the polynomial in terms of its roots:\n\\[\na(x - 3)(x + 2)(x - r) = 0.\n\\]\n\nFirst, we expand \\((x - 3)(x + 2)\\):\n\\[\n(x - 3)(x + 2) = x^2 + 2x - 3x - 6 = x^2 - x - 6.\n\\]\n\nNext, we multiply this result by \\((x - r)\\):\n\\[\n(x^2 - x - 6)(x - r) = x^3 - rx^2 - x^2 + rx - 6x + 6r = x^3 - (r+1)x^2 + (r-6)x + 6r.\n\\]\n\nSince this must equal \\( ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d \\), we can equate the coefficients from both expressions:\n\\[\nax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = x^3 - (r+1)x^2 + (r-6)x + 6r.\n\\]\n\nFrom this, we identify the coefficients:\n\\[\na = a,\n\\]\n\\[\nb = -(r+1),\n\\]\n\\[\nc = r-6,\n\\]\n\\[\nd = 6r.\n\\]\n\nWe need to find \\(\\frac{b+c}{a}\\):\n\\[\nb + c = -(r+1) + (r-6) = -r - 1 + r - 6 = -7.\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\\[\n\\frac{b+c}{a} = \\frac{-7}{a}.\n\\]\n\nSince we do not have a specific value for \\(a\\), the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-7}.\n\\]",
